==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Originally spelled {{m|en|RADAR}}; an {{acronym of|en|[[radio|'''ra'''dio]] [[detection|'''d'''etection]] [[and|'''a'''nd]] [[ranging|'''r'''anging]]|nocap=1}} {{coin|en|the United States Navy|w=United States Navy|in=1940|nobycat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹeɪ.dɑː(ɹ)/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹeɪ.dɑɹ/|[ˈɹeɪ.ɾɑɹ]|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-radar.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A method of [[detecting]] [[distant]] [[object]]s and [[determining]] their [[position]], [[velocity]], or other [[characteristic]]s by [[analysis]] of sent [[radio]] [[wave]]s (usually [[microwave]]s) [[reflect]]ed from their [[surface]]s
#: {{ux|en|The enemy fleet was able to be found using '''radar'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A type of [[system]] using such a method, [[differentiate]]d by [[platform]], [[configuration]], [[frequency]], [[power]], and other [[technical]] [[attribute]]s.
# {{lb|en|countable}} An [[installation]] of such a system or of the [[transmit]]ting and [[receive|receiving]] [[apparatus]].
# {{lb|en|countable|figuratively}} A [[superior]] [[ability]] to [[detect]] something.
#: {{ux|en|His sensitive '''radar''' for hidden alliances keeps him out of trouble.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=29 April 2021|author=Jamie Jackson|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2021/apr/29/manchester-united-roma-europa-league-semi-final-first-leg-match-report|work=The Guardian|title=Edinson Cavani and Bruno Fernandes help Manchester United hit Roma for six|passage=It came inside 50 minutes and moments later Cavani should have had a 12th. Pogba and Shaw combined before the left-back's cross teed up the striker but his '''radar''' was awry.}}

